{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells","id":1207688,"title":"Does anyone actually use Aimed Spells?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-16T10:04:31-07:00","id":1207688,"title":"Does anyone actually use Aimed Spells?","content":"By anyone, I mean players or Storytellers with actual play experience, not theoretical mages within the setting. I've played a <i>lot</i> of second edition Mage and it's never been used once, but all of those games were with the same players so it might just be a bias all of us share and not as universal as I'm assuming.<br /> <br /> So if this is a thing you've done (especially as a player), I want to know!<br /> If, like us, you've always avoided it, I'd like to know that, too - and what your reasons have been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T10:57:52-07:00","id":1207708,"title":"","content":"Our Adamantine Arrow had a lot of Athletics so relied on it a few times when they couldn't spare enough Reach for Cast-by-Sensory. They usually didn't mind overReaching (mechanically, it's not that bad) but sometimes there were situational factors that made it not the best choice, usually when other mages were around or Abyssal entities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T12:11:24-07:00","id":1207723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1207708#post1207708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our Adamantine Arrow had a lot of Athletics so relied on it a few times when they couldn't spare enough Reach for Cast-by-Sensory. They usually didn't mind overReaching (mechanically, it's not that bad) but sometimes there were situational factors that made it not the best choice, usually when other mages were around or Abyssal entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>How often was missing the spell actually an issue? <br /> <br /> I think that's the main thing that has stopped us from using it; containing Paradox might give you some Conditions or worse, but generally, you can at least count on the spell still working as intended, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T12:35:01-07:00","id":1207728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1207723#post1207723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often was missing the spell actually an issue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just one as far as I can recall. After that they tended to throw not at a target but someplace near them, catching them in its effect and avoiding the Defense problem. Basically if you have good Athletics (or Firearms), it saves you a Reach, the Arrow never got the 'ignores Defense' Merit because they didn't have the Arcana prereq (Time, I think) but if she had that I imagine she'd rely on it a lot more..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that's the main thing that has stopped us from using it; containing Paradox might give you some Conditions or worse, but generally, you can at least count on the spell still working as intended, at least. </div> </div> </div>That's funny, it's supposed to be the first problem with Paradox, because the easiest thing for Paradox to do to a spell is alter its Reach specifications. That ended up popping up a lot, as one Paradox Reach was probably the average. No one had ever gotten 5, which was what was needed to 'accidentally' summon an Abyssal entity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-16-2018, 03:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T13:07:02-07:00","id":1207738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1207728#post1207728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's funny, it's supposed to be the first problem with Paradox, because the easiest thing for Paradox to do to a spell is alter its Reach specifications.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is a result of another of my group's biases, I can count the Paradoxes they've Released on one hand. That fear comes from the same place - having their magic undone or pointed at the wrong person.<br /> <br /> So they just go with the option where that can't generally happen, which is attempting to contain it (since even a failed Containment won't generally mess with the Reach of the current spell). I'm trying to revisit how I handle all of these options to include a little more variety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T13:16:37-07:00","id":1207740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1207738#post1207738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this is a result of another of my group's biases, I can count the Paradoxes they've Released on one hand. That fear comes from the same place - having their magic undone or pointed at the wrong person.<br /> <br /> So they just go with the option where that can't generally happen, which is attempting to contain it (since even a failed Containment won't generally mess with the Reach of the current spell). I'm trying to revisit how I handle all of these options to include a little more variety.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think keeping track of Mana can help, as well as not having 'one encounter in the middle of nowhere then everyone stops for the day' types of encounters. I asked once and apparently some STs are really free with the Mana, letting everyone just get full between sessions or rests, but even with a full Hallow if you're active and casting spells, especially outside of your major Arcana, you can blow through Mana pretty fast, which makes it harder to use to reduce Paradox. And obviously the encounter thing is something that's just going to need to come up, you can't have everything be wave after wave of danger, but Bashing heals pretty fast, so it's easy to soak the Paradox rather than risk it if you are, say, just casting a spell to make the gas station attendant fill you up on a road trip and aren't going to be dealing with more magic for the next several hours. Our last sessions ended on a sort of dungeon crawl in enemy territory and they couldn't exactly take a break to heal up their Bashing and things got very tense at the climax.<br /> <br /> But even then, getting someone to more consistently use Aimed spells would probably take a very specific kind of character, with at least some better Athletics or Firearms. It's a more actiony type of spellslinger. I think someone made a gunslinger legacy that relied on it, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-16-2018, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T15:31:48-07:00","id":1207778,"title":"","content":"Had a dungeon run a couple nights ago, the only time I spent mana was for like 2 time spells (Life/Space mage) everything else I could improv in primary arcana and then the changeling decided he didn't like my face and drained all my mana and sent me to the hedge (in a place where any kind of speed or teleporting was shut down because infinite stat god machine)<br /> <br /> Even when I cast spells left and right, I think I risked a chance die paradox maybe twice the entire session, and spent like 3 mana the entire session until the changeling ate it all and fill the reward room with hedge thorns. I was in a ban, and he said &quot;nah, I don't even need to sense you as long as you're technically in the same scene you're done for. I'll get you after my rage is done, also it works even though every realm tied to this place also has any movement oriented effects shut down.&quot; So that was hair raising, and my character certainly had some stern words for him.<br /> <br /> Also why bother aiming a spell without the adamantine hand merit. If I'm rolling athletics I might as well be firing my bow or running out of their range/into cover. A mage with a dedicated tool handy should be able to cast with 1-2 reach really reliably unless they're casting spells a bit above their ability (ie you get your 4th dot of Life, and you're casting the damage spell you just learned at sensory range instant cast constantly over and over gradually building paradox.) Mage is honestly more elegant than just direct damage spells I've only run into a couple encounters either I or the other mage couldn't incapacitate our foes in 3 spells or less. The boss was obviously hard, but it also had upwards of 20 or more dice for just about everything and 17 defense lol. The DM had clearly had enough of us xD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","user":"Arduras","date":". 04-16-2018, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T19:09:10-07:00","id":1207839,"title":"","content":"Something to remember: Every time Paradox is invoked in a scene, it adds a +1 to their Paradox. In really intense scenes, that can add up pretty fast. I finished a scene not too long ago where my Thyrsus was eating ten Paradox dice on some rolls. In the end, she nearly died because she couldn't risk casting a healing spell to heal herself without making it worse.<br /> <br /> If you only expect to need to risk one Paradox in a given scene, there's not much mechanical reason not to take the risk, but when your back is to a wall, it gets tense very quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T19:09:51-07:00","id":1207840,"title":"","content":"I have used Aim on more than one occasion. Ended up missing about 80% so not bad. In another game I played a Mage that had fast spell and alot of other stuff that helped me hit what i aimed for. That character was alot of fun also.<br /> <br /> I was even looking into making a custom legacy that revolved around spell slinging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 04-16-2018, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T23:41:41-07:00","id":1207902,"title":"","content":"Players I've played/run games with/for tended to approach the situation as Inodivs group, at least once the system had been understood. Aimed spells are only used when there is little consequence to the spell not &quot;hitting&quot;. I think one Acanthus player in a game of mine even took the fast spells merit and still never used it.<br /> <br /> Same for Paradox, I've yet to see a spell let loose from a mage who knows how to contain a paradox IC. Personally I houserule that the spells still can run amok if you fail the containment roll, so that works out fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-17T21:09:18-07:00","id":1208311,"title":"","content":"I've never seen Aiming used in the 15 sessions I've run, but partly because players typically forget about the mechanic.<br /> <br /> On the issue of Reach &amp; Paradox I think that 2e is better than 1e in this regard for making the consequences harsher for over-Reaching, but it's maybe still a little too easy to Reach into whatever you need.<br /> <br /> Typically it might go something like this in any give scene:<br /> <br /> Spell 1: Over reaching by one - dedicated tool = chance die for Paradox<br /> Spell 2: Over reaching by one + 1 for earlier Paradox chance - dedicated tool = chance die for Paradox<br /> Spell 3: 1 + 2 - DT = 1 die (not likely)<br /> Spell 4: 2 dice (50/50)<br /> Spell 5: 3 dice - Probably had to deal with a small Paradox easily contained by Wisdom<br /> <br /> I mean you aren't really affected until you're 5 Spells in and that's if you even over-Reach 5 times in a row instead of interspersing some other things in between.<br /> <br /> The net result for my players is that they've had maybe 2 or 3 Resistance Bashing each maximum in any given Scene.<br /> <br /> Now, to be fair one of my players ended up going into resistant lethal due to damage wrap-around and he's been carrying the wounds for a few sessions now. I had a talk with him and he agreed to take a Persistent social Condition from permanent scaring from that fight, just for the coolness factor.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that the rules need changing necessarily, but beginning players aren't going to worry to much about Paradox IMO. It's more flavour than anything else.<br /> <br /> I don't have any experience with Gnosis 3 characters, so I'm not sure how well using Mana to mitigate the potentially larger Paradox pools works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 04-18-2018, 12:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T04:15:37-07:00","id":1208391,"title":"","content":"Yeah, and even with the above examples you can spend mana to reduce paradox dice 1 for 1 so it really never comes up outside of the chance die unless I'm _really trying to get paradox_ lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T16:05:50-07:00","id":1208616,"title":"","content":"Aimed spells having to use area of effect scale makes it a very niche thing to do. Also what if the area is big enough that if you throw the spell between two targets you can impact both. Is the roll just Gnosis + Firearms/Athletics since a spot on the ground has no defense? And if so why would you ever want to throw an aimed spell at something rather than just near it? The idea that a person in the same room as you gets defense vs a room sized area effect when you can just throw the spell at your feet to affect him (and you unless fated to ignore it etc) is odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 04-18-2018, 07:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T19:26:19-07:00","id":1208669,"title":"","content":"But then if you don't make the area large enough people can dive for cover. And if you do you're going to be taking a lot more dice penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T20:48:47-07:00","id":1208701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1208669#post1208669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then if you don't make the area large enough people can dive for cover. And if you do you're going to be taking a lot more dice penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they're behind cover they can be out of sensory range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-18T21:29:53-07:00","id":1208712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1208616#post1208616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aimed spells having to use area of effect scale makes it a very niche thing to do. Also what if the area is big enough that if you throw the spell between two targets you can impact both. Is the roll just Gnosis + Firearms/Athletics since a spot on the ground has no defense? And if so why would you ever want to throw an aimed spell at something rather than just near it? The idea that a person in the same room as you gets defense vs a room sized area effect when you can just throw the spell at your feet to affect him (and you unless fated to ignore it etc) is odd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably to avoid things like fireballing the floor instead of burning only one guy, and ending up with making an area where people who enter it turn into frogs instead of turning one guy into a frog.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T01:21:55-07:00","id":1208759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1208712#post1208712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably to avoid things like fireballing the floor instead of burning only one guy, and ending up with making an area where people who enter it turn into frogs instead of turning one guy into a frog.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would it avoid this? If the spell also has a duration longer than 1 turn then you can aim and throw a &quot;Everybody in this area turns into a frog spell&quot;.<br /> If i just want to throw a spell big enough to affect 3 enemies into the next room do i just roll gnosis+firearms/athletics to make sure i get the spell through the door? Does failing the roll mean i drop it at my feet and the spell affects the room i am in instead? Do i need to make 3 rolls one for each intended subject? If the spell has duration then that spell affects anybody entering that area as normal.<br /> What about if i am just fireballing a subject but it just happens that its within arms reach of another subject so the spell would affect both, this other subject is immobile and probably doesnt get defense, surely i can just fireball them and not take a defense penalty and my spell will still affect my original target if i succeed. Swap that subject with a inanimate pole which probably also doesnt have defense and why not just fireball the pole and catch the original subject in the area?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T02:00:28-07:00","id":1208770,"title":"","content":"As usual, the following is my personal rulings, but anyways...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1208759#post1208759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would it avoid this? If the spell also has a duration longer than 1 turn then you can aim and throw a &amp;quot;Everybody in this area turns into a frog spell&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? You need Duration longer than 1 turn to Aim? That\u2019s... something new. I may have to reread if that\u2019s the case. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If i just want to throw a spell big enough to affect 3 enemies into the next room do i just roll gnosis+firearms/athletics to make sure i get the spell through the door? </div> </div> </div>You don\u2019t need to Aim for the targets if you don\u2019t mind burning the room as well. (Although since this is fire we\u2019re talking about, it\u2019ll spread a bit)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does failing the roll mean i drop it at my feet and the spell affects the room i am in instead? </div> </div> </div>Depending on the Storyteller. That sounds more like a dramatic failure, though. I imagine most rulings will be that it just missed and fizzled away or something. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do i need to make 3 rolls one for each intended subject? </div> </div> </div>Only if you\u2019re Aiming for each target. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the spell has duration then that spell affects anybody entering that area as normal.<br /> What about if i am just fireballing a subject but it just happens that its within arms reach of another subject so the spell would affect both, this other subject is immobile and probably doesnt get defense, surely i can just fireball them and not take a defense penalty and my spell will still affect my original target if i succeed. Swap that subject with a inanimate pole which probably also doesnt have defense and why not just fireball the pole and catch the original subject in the area? </div> </div> </div>I see it like this; Yes you can, but should you? Haphazardly throwing spells at everything that gets in the way just because it\u2019d be more efficient isn\u2019t exactly safe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T02:14:35-07:00","id":1208774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1208770#post1208770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As usual, the following is my personal rulings, but anyways...<br /> Huh? You need Duration longer than 1 turn to Aim? That\u2019s... something new. I may have to reread if that\u2019s the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said IF a spell has a longer duration it doesnt avoid &quot;making an area where people who enter it turn into frogs instead of turning one guy into a frog.&quot; which is what you posted?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only if you\u2019re Aiming for each target. </div> </div> </div>Thats just it though im not aiming for each target, im aiming at no targets, the peeps just happen to be in the area of the spell when it hits a target (ie the room). Rolling gnosis+firearms/athletics for each target caught in the area of affect isnt stated anywhere and seems counter productive is there is no way they can avoid the spell without getting out the area first (reflexively moving out the room would work)<br /> <br /> Raw says that if you fail the roll the spell misses the subject but by how much, and what if missing the subject just isnt possible. If i throw a campus sized spell in front of me so that im not in the area of affect, even if i miss the guy 10 feet directly in front of me with the spell it'll affect him where ever the spell lands?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T02:50:03-07:00","id":1208782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1208774#post1208774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If i throw a campus sized spell in front of me so that im not in the area of affect, even if i miss the guy 10 feet directly in front of me with the spell it'll affect him where ever the spell lands?</div> </div> </div> </div>In this specific case, just put the spell in front of you instead of throwing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T03:05:16-07:00","id":1208786,"title":"","content":"You still need to hit an area (Arm\u2019s reach from a central point) the size of your arms reach, the default area scale of 1 unless you put a reach into it to increase the size, but at that point you may as well cast it as sensory. So that area isn't the room, and therefore still needs to hit the target. That is how I see it and your opinion may differ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T04:07:55-07:00","id":1208792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1208782#post1208782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this specific case, just put the spell in front of you instead of throwing it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what if you dont?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You still need to hit an area (Arm\u2019s reach from a central point) the size of your arms reach, the default area scale of 1 unless you put a reach into it to increase the size, but at that point you may as well cast it as sensory </div> </div> </div>Not so, its only a -2 penalty to go from arms reach to small room. There is no reach involved which is important if we are talking about why somebody is aiming a spell instead of sensory ranging it. Im happy that a roll to hit a room is just gnosis+firearms/athletics. I can see an argument for allowing defense vs an arms reach area effect maybe if people also get defense vs grenades? Id have to look it up but do people get defense if a grenade goes off nearby? If they do then thats fine, if they dont they why do they get it vs a spell. <br /> <br /> So after reading hurt locker about grenades, it says defense only works if bolstered by supernatural speed. I would argue this also applies to thrown area spells. Unless the opponent is fast enough to get outside the area he doesnt get defense?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T05:38:30-07:00","id":1208816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1208774#post1208774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said IF a spell has a longer duration it doesnt avoid &amp;quot;making an area where people who enter it turn into frogs instead of turning one guy into a frog.&amp;quot; which is what you posted?<br /> <br /> Thats just it though im not aiming for each target, im aiming at no targets, the peeps just happen to be in the area of the spell when it hits a target (ie the room). Rolling gnosis+firearms/athletics for each target caught in the area of affect isnt stated anywhere and seems counter productive is there is no way they can avoid the spell without getting out the area first (reflexively moving out the room would work)<br /> <br /> Raw says that if you fail the roll the spell misses the subject but by how much, and what if missing the subject just isnt possible. If i throw a campus sized spell in front of me so that im not in the area of affect, even if i miss the guy 10 feet directly in front of me with the spell it'll affect him where ever the spell lands?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Wait a sec... does the book even allow Aiming at empty space in the first place like you\u2019d do with a grenade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T05:42:09-07:00","id":1208819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1208816#post1208816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh. Wait a sec... does the book even allow Aiming at empty space in the first place like you\u2019d do with a grenade?</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume yes, because it\u2019s no different than casting a spell on any empty area except that it leaves your hand.<br /> <br /> I personally find it a bit weird you have to target an area instead of a subject in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-19-2018, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T06:00:04-07:00","id":1208826,"title":"","content":"I don't really see the problem? If you just want to throw a small room sized fireball into a room, you aim at the center and go, no defense applied to the roll. If you want to burn the feet of just that one person running away from you: defense applies. If you don't hit, you might hurt somebody else you didn't want to. So as long as you don't care for collateral damage, than yes, defense is not really an issue. Pretty clearly a Wisdom issue though, if you rather often burn down whole buildings just to get that one person in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 04-19-2018, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T06:29:14-07:00","id":1208832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1208826#post1208826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see the problem? If you just want to throw a small room sized fireball into a room, you aim at the center and go, no defense applied to the roll. If you want to burn the feed of just that one person running away from you: defense applies. If you don't hit, you might hurt somebody else you didn't want to. So as long as you don't care for collateral damage, than yes, defense is not really an issue. Pretty clearly a Wisdom issue though, if you rather often burn down whole buildings just to get that one person in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this seems to be the closest thing to an answer this issue has.<br /> <br /> Note to self; swap out sensory range for other Reach options when revisiting past stuff in my Legacies thread, unless it\u2019s supposed to use sympathy, cuz I\u2019ve been underrating Aimed spells it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 04-19-2018, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T14:21:50-07:00","id":1209010,"title":"","content":"Yeah. -2 to bake a whole room is pretty sweet. I would allow a dive for cover similar to dodging if there was room to do so. A small room is about 15 x 15 feet so someone should be able to dive out of range if they take their action to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T16:10:54-07:00","id":1209041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1209010#post1209010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. -2 to bake a whole room is pretty sweet. I would allow a dive for cover similar to dodging if there was room to do so. A small room is about 15 x 15 feet so someone should be able to dive out of range if they take their action to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could drop prone but moving in reaction to &quot;ranged attacks&quot; is actually the first dot of Close Quarters iirc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T17:03:10-07:00","id":1209055,"title":"","content":"Meh. Every other RPG has Dive for Cover rules so I think WoD should have them as well. I don't think you should need a special merit to attempt to dive away from a clearly incoming projectile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1470,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","user":"Johnny Awesome","date":". 04-19-2018, 08:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T17:30:48-07:00","id":1209068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1209055#post1209055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. Every other RPG has Dive for Cover rules so I think WoD should have them as well. I don't think you should need a special merit to attempt to dive away from a clearly incoming projectile.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends, magic is only visible to things that can &quot;See&quot; it (ie mage sight) otherwise it's wholly invisible until it takes effect (unless you will otherwise, like forcing your nimbus so that it shows for everyone) But short of making a fireball and throwing it you could simply throw the &quot;ignite&quot; symbol into a room or something similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T18:09:59-07:00","id":1209078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Johnny Awesome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1207688-does-anyone-actually-use-aimed-spells?p=1209055#post1209055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh. Every other RPG has Dive for Cover rules so I think WoD should have them as well. I don't think you should need a special merit to attempt to dive away from a clearly incoming projectile.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well they have, it's called Defence, it however doesn't give the same mechanical benefits of being able to get into Cover out of turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-19T21:39:44-07:00","id":1209116,"title":"","content":"Chronicles has dropping prone, which gives a minor benefit to Defense and potentially more if there's something in front of you. And you can do it before your turn, but it uses up your action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-20T12:24:40-07:00","id":1209351,"title":"","content":"I'm probably going to allow a Dodge roll where if you roll more successes than the attacker's aim roll you get to dive out of the way at the cost of your action as long as the limit of your movement would allow you to clear the blast radius.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}